---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---
<Layout
  title="Hanfu in Xi'an: Rental, Photoshoot & Where to Wear It"
  description="Hanfu rental in Xi'an: prices, where to rent near Yongningmen, the best photoshoot spots (City Wall, Tang Paradise, Big Wild Goose Pagoda), and a full 3-day itinerary."
  canonicalUrl="https://www.dresses-hanfu.com/travel/xian/"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Travel", url: "/travel" }, { name: "Xi'an", url: "/travel/xian" }]}
  articleSchema={{
    datePublished: "2026-08-01",
    dateModified: "2026-08-08",
    author: { "@type": "Person", "name": "Hanfu Dress Guide Editorial Team" }
  }}
>
  <SiteHeader active="/travel" />
  <main>
    <article>
      <section class="section" style="padding-bottom: 2rem;">
        <div class="container-narrow">
          <p style="font-size:0.8125rem;color:var(--color-muted);margin-bottom:1rem;"><a href="/" style="color:var(--color-accent);">Home</a> &rsaquo; <a href="/travel/" style="color:var(--color-accent);">Travel</a> &rsaquo; Xi'an</p>
          <h1>Hanfu in Xi'an: Rental, Photoshoot &amp; Where to Wear It</h1>
          <p class="lead" style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--color-muted);margin-top:1.5rem;line-height:1.55;">
            Xi'an is the most complete Hanfu experience in China. Ancient walls, a Tang-dynasty theme park, and hundreds of rental shops within walking distance of each other. If you only visit one city for Hanfu, make it this one.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
        <div class="container-narrow">
          <h2>Quick Facts</h2>
          <div style="overflow-x:auto;">
            <table class="size-ref-table" style="margin-top:1rem;">
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><strong>Rental price</strong></td><td>100–200 RMB (~$14–28 USD) for 24h</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Hair &amp; makeup</strong></td><td>Usually included in the rental price</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Deposit</strong></td><td>200–500 RMB, returned when you bring the outfit back</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Rental period</strong></td><td>Full day (24h) is standard; half-day often available</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Peak season</strong></td><td>Spring (Mar–Apr) and autumn (Sep–Oct) weekends</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
        <div class="container-narrow">
          <h2>Where to Rent</h2>
          <p class="text-muted">
            Rental shops cluster around <strong>Yongningmen (South Gate) on the City Wall</strong> and around <strong>Big Wild Goose Pagoda square</strong>. These are shop districts, not single stores — prices and quality vary by 20–30%, so walk a couple of blocks and compare before committing.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            Shops near the South Gate tend to have English-speaking staff and bigger catalogs; the Wild Goose Pagoda cluster is more convenient if your photos are all in that area. Both do styling on-site, which takes 30–60 minutes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
        <div class="container-narrow">
          <h2>Best Spots for Hanfu Photos</h2>
          <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--color-muted);font-size:0.9375rem;line-height:1.8;">
            <li><strong>City Wall at sunset</strong> — arrive by 16:30–17:00. Golden light against grey brick, with the old city on one side and modern Xi'an on the other. Corner towers are the best framing.</li>
            <li><strong>Tang Paradise</strong> — Tang-dynasty gardens made for big-sleeve silhouettes. Mid-morning for soft light, or evening for lanterns.</li>
            <li><strong>Big Wild Goose Pagoda</strong> — the classic pagoda + reflection pool shot. Early morning, before crowds.</li>
            <li><strong>Grand Tang Mall at night</strong> — the giant lantern-and-light display is unforgettable in Hanfu. Go after 19:00.</li>
            <li><strong>Shaanxi History Museum (outside)</strong> — clean architectural lines; free backdrop near the rental district.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
        <div class="container-narrow">
          <h2>What It Actually Costs</h2>
          <div style="overflow-x:auto;">
            <table class="size-ref-table" style="margin-top:1rem;">
              <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Typical Range</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Hanfu rental (24h)</td><td>100–200 RMB (~$14–28)</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Hairstyling</td><td>Usually included</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Photographer (2h)</td><td>400–800 RMB (~$55–110)</td></tr>
                <tr><td>City Wall ticket</td><td>54 RMB (~$8)</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Tang Paradise ticket</td><td>120 RMB (~$17)</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Big Wild Goose Pagoda</td><td>50–85 RMB depending on sections</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-muted);margin-top:0.75rem;">A full day with mid-range rental, styling, and a 2-hour photographer session lands around 800–1,500 RMB (~$110–210 USD) per person.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
        <div class="container-narrow">
          <h2>3-Day Xi'an Hanfu Itinerary</h2>

          <h3 style="margin-top:1.5rem;">Day 1 — Arrival &amp; Rental Fitting</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">Arrive in the afternoon and head to the rental district near Yongningmen. Browse 3–4 shops to compare styles and prices. Get fitted — the shop handles sizing and hairstyling (30–60 minutes). Book a photographer for tomorrow if you want one: 400–800 RMB for a 2-hour session.</p>

          <h3 style="margin-top:1.5rem;">Day 2 — City Wall &amp; Tang Paradise</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">Morning: arrive at the City Wall (Yongningmen entrance) by 8:30 AM. Walk or cycle the wall in Hanfu — corner towers are the best photos. Afternoon: Tang Paradise gardens for Tang-dynasty backdrops. Evening: the Grand Tang Mall light show, still in Hanfu. Allow 2–3 hours total for makeup touch-ups at the rental shop.</p>

          <h3 style="margin-top:1.5rem;">Day 3 — Big Wild Goose Pagoda &amp; Departure</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">Morning: Big Wild Goose Pagoda and the reflection pool — the classic shot. Afternoon: return the rental (most are 24-hour) and explore the Muslim Quarter for street food. Total for 3 days including rental, styling, and photography: roughly 800–1,500 RMB (~$110–210 USD) per person.</p>

          <h3 style="margin-top:1.5rem;">Practical Notes</h3>
          <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--color-muted);font-size:0.9375rem;line-height:1.8;">
            <li><strong>Booking</strong> — walk-ins are fine outside peak weekends; book 1–2 days ahead in spring/autumn.</li>
            <li><strong>Passport</strong> — bring it; most shops need it as ID for the deposit.</li>
            <li><strong>Return time</strong> — most rentals are 24 hours from pickup; late returns cost a half-day fee.</li>
            <li><strong>Language</strong> — South Gate shops usually have English speakers; otherwise use a translation app.</li>
            <li><strong>Collar rule</strong> — cross right over left. See <a href="/guides/how-to-wear/" style="color:var(--color-accent);">How to Wear Hanfu</a>.</li>
          </ul>

          <div style="margin-top:3rem;padding:2rem;background:var(--color-accent-light);border-radius:var(--radius-md);">
            <p style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;font-family:var(--font-display);">Next Steps</p>
            <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.75rem;margin-top:1rem;">
              <a href="/travel/" class="btn btn-outline">All City Guides</a>
              <a href="/guides/how-to-wear/" class="btn btn-outline">How to Wear Hanfu</a>
              <a href="/travel/hangzhou/" class="btn btn-outline">Hangzhou Guide</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>
